{"kind":"artifact","text":"Merged: event numbers on every surface, on main at 88b51864.\n\nEvery durable event carries a sequence derived from the fold's own record index, and the surfaces name events by it. The bounded CLI status and the full renderer print #N for commitment requests, artifact events, review reports and ineffective decisions; the browser already did. Git commits, actor fingerprints and the frontier hash stay abbreviated, and that asymmetry is deliberate — git resolves an abbreviated commit, and nothing resolves an abbreviated event.\n\nThe legacy demo page is gone. It was a second renderer of the same projection that no reader could reach, still abbreviating events after the browser had stopped, and a surface nobody visits is a surface nobody corrects. A test fails if it returns.\n\nTwo regressions guard the naming, one per renderer, each verified to fail when its own abbreviation is restored.\n\nThe head is 88b51864 rather than the merge commit a3f416ec, because the merge left the tree inconsistent and one more commit was needed. Both parents had rebuilt internal/service/uidist, so git resolved that generated file by choosing a side, and the result was an embed built from neither the merged source nor either parent. `make ui-check` catches it; nothing runs between merge and push, so it caught it only because I ran it by hand. The rebuild is committed and the gate is green at this head.\n\nSuccessor to f44bb842, the reviewed branch artifact.","body":{"commit":"88b5186461a57d6671ab24d995d45e910ac875ea","path":"internal/workroom"}}